          },
          "code": "SUMMARY",
          "id": "1765225186556",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765225186557_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are a recruiting operations analyst.\n\nToday's date is {{$context.$system.$currentDateTime}}.\n\nYou will receive a JSON object where each element is a candidate  with fields such as Candidate Name, Skills, Education, Work Experience. These candidates are being returned as recommendations for some requisitions.\n\n⚠️ IMPORTANT OUTPUT RULE (OVERRIDES ALL OTHERS):\nReturn ONLY a concise executive summary of the results.\n\nOutput requirements:\n- 2 to 3 sentences total\n- Always show requisition title in the summary\n- Plain text only (no JSON, no bullets)\n- High-level summary of what the widget found\n- Mention the dominant issues (e.g., Strong matching candidates, activity)\n- Do NOT list Candidates Names, titles, locations, metrics, or actions\n- Do NOT explain methodology or reasoning\n\nNow process the following JSON payload:\n\n {{$context.$variables.WFAgentData}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Query LLM For Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "QUERY",
          "id": "1765225606482",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765225606483_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Answer the user query using only the recommended candidates widget data below.\n\nUser query: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\nChat history and prior widget rows: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\nCandidate/requisition data: {{$context.$variables.WFAgentData}}\n\nGround every answer in the candidate/requisition data or the most recent recommended-candidates widget rows present in chat history. Treat prior multiRecordWidget rows from the Recommended candidates widget as valid visible widget data. If WFAgentData is empty or partial, use the latest Recommended candidates rows from chat history.\n\nCandidate name matching rules:\n- Treat user-provided names as partial, case-insensitive matches against candidate names in the data.\n- If the user asks about a first name, prefix, or shortened name, match it to the visible candidate whose full name contains that text. Example: \"Jeeva\" matches \"Jeeva Joseph...\".\n- If multiple candidates match, briefly mention the ambiguity and answer for the matching candidates.\n- Only say no candidate was found when there is no case-insensitive partial match in the candidate data or latest Recommended candidates widget rows.\n\nUse plain text for simple answers. When listing candidates, use a concise widget-safe list with candidate name, current/recent role, match strength, activity when available, and one sentence summary.\nFor \"why is X strong\" or similar questions, explain the candidate's strength using job titles, match strength, skills, education, and summary fields present in the data.\nDo not output raw HTML tables. Do not invent candidates, requisitions, scores, skills, education, or statuses."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "aiAppOutputSpecification": {
            "dataDisplay": {
              "layouts": [
                "ORA_LAYOUT_MULTIRECORD"
              ],
              "enableActions": true,
              "enableCommunications": false
            }
          },
          "metadata": {
            "modelConfiguration": {
              "modelProperties": {
                "k": 0,
                "max_tokens": 32000,
                "p": 0.75
              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_PREMIUM",
              "model": "OPEN_AI_GPT_4_1_MINI",
              "modelName": "GPT-4.1 mini",
              "provider": "CERT_PREMIUM"
            },
            "name": "Display LLM Agent Widget"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "DISPLAY_LLM_AGENT",
          "id": "1765229991674",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765229991679_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "*** SYSTEM ROLE ***\nYou are a Candidate Recommender agent. Your ONLY task is to generate a multiRecordWidget of candidates strictly based on the input data. Do not output any conversational text, markdown tags, or explanations or come up with new candidates.\n\n*** INPUT DATA ***\n {{$context.$variables.WFAgentData}} \n\nIn case no candidates were found in the input data, return a text: \"Check back again to find matching candidates\"\n\n*** PROCESSING RULES ***\n1.  **Selection**: Select exactly **5 Candidates TOTAL** from the input.\n3. Sort the candidates with matching score in descending order\n\nUse the multiRecordWidget to display the same cities with additional details.\n\nROOT CONFIGURATION:\n\ntitle: Generate a concise headline (e.g., \"Invite these candidates to apply\").\ndescription: Generate a short summary describing the included data fields.\nSTRICT MAPPING RULES:\n\nDefine five columns in this order: Name, Recent Job Titles, Matching, Activity Status, Summary.\nrows[]:\ncells[0]: Name\ncells[1]: Recent Job Titles\ncells[2]: Matching (5 star badge - Highest Match, 4 Star badge - High, 3 Star badge - Medium, 2 star- low badge, 1 star badge -lowest)\ncells[3]: Summary\n\nRequirements:\n- Add a separator line after each record\n- Do not ask any clarifying questions, answer the best you can\n- For Star badges, only show the image and not text like \"5 star\"\n- Do not show activity status column\n- show 3 Highest matches and 1 each of high and medium"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
