          "metadata": {
            "name": "Parse Actions LLM"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "end"
          },
          "code": "PARSE_ACTIONS_LLM",
          "id": "1765930272978",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765930272980_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Your job is to provide the list of actions. This is a Talent Advisor agent for a recruiter sourcing candidates for a recruitment application... The data on which you need to choose the best actions would be from here - \n\nData Object: {{$context.$variables.WFAgentData}} \n- Get the list of 5 candidates and put their personIds in PersonIds, \n- Get the RequisitionId from the data object and put it in RequisitionId\n\nEnsure the followUp Command always have ora.Invoke has the same format as in the example. You can substitute only the properties - key value pair but not change the signature. Use only IDs from the data object; never copy placeholder IDs from examples.  \n\nYou will only support 1 actions and their name and code are as follows. Keep the action name under 10 characters - \n\n1. Action Name - Invite to Apply , Action Code - AddProspect\n- This action takes in a requisition and adds the persons being recommended to that requisition as Prospects. \n- In the followUpCommand Payload pass the RequisitionId and the List of PersonIds for the candidates as per the contract below.\n- Always include action code in payload -> AddProspect\n\n- Display 1  action with candidate with Invite to Apply\n\nYou can send actions back as part of your response. Actions follow this format:\n\n{\n  \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#\",\n  \"type\": \"object\",\n  \"properties\": {\n    \"title\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The main title of the notification. Must be a concise phrase, under 10 words.  Don't display the requisitions Title\"\n    },\n    \"shortDescription\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"A brief description of the notification, written as a single, complete sentence.\"\n    },\n    \"actionText\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"The text to display on the action button.\"\n    },\n    \"followUpCommand\": {\n      \"type\": \"string\",\n      \"description\": \"A command string to be executed. Must follow one of three standardized formats: ora.App.*(params) or ora.Agent(content). The exact content will be specified by the prompting instructions.\"\n    },\n    \"priority\": {\n      \"type\": \"boolean\",\n      \"description\": \"Optional. Controls whether this action should be prioritized in the display. If undefined or false, the action will not be prioritized. Only when set to true will the action be prioritized. By default, omit this property or set it to false unless your prompting explicitly instructs you to prioritize the action.\"\n    }\n  },\n  \"required\": [\"title\", \"shortDescription\", \"actionText\", \"followUpCommand\"],\n  \"additionalProperties\": false\n}\n\nAlways return the ActionCode in the followUpCommand.\n\nAs an example:\n\n{\n  \"title\": \"Invite to Apply\",\n  \"shortDescription\": \"Adds the candidate to as a prospect to a requisition\" ,\n  \"actionText\": \"Invite to Apply\",\n  \"followUpCommand\": \"ora.Invoke( \\\"AddProspect\\\", {\\\"RequisitionId\\\": \\\"<REQUISITION_ID_FROM_DATA>\\\", \\\"PersonIds\\\": [\\\"<PERSON_ID_1>\\\", \\\"<PERSON_ID_2>\\\", \\\"<PERSON_ID_3>\\\", \\\"<PERSON_ID_4>\\\", \\\"<PERSON_ID_5>\\\"]})\"\n}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
